---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Brand Strategy &amp; Identity Design | Kelp Agency"
  description={
    "Branding is more than a logo and making things look good. Your branding should bring clarity to what you do and why."
  }
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Content Creation Services"
    title="Branding"
    description="Branding is more than a logo and making things look good. Your branding should bring clarity to what you do and why."
    lottieFile="branding.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Why branding matters</h2>
      <p>
        We all have the opportunity to build a brand that lasts. Whether you’re
        starting out or looking for new ways in which your company can grow, our
        services will help guide and promote not only what makes YOU unique but
        also bring attention from consumers who want more of those qualities as
        well!
      </p>
      <p>
        In many cases, Branding may reach more people than a business’s product
        itself. This is because branding can be applied to more than just
        physical products. Branding is used in every main component of customer
        contact. From posts on social media, to ads on the radio, to the boxes a
        product ships in, a brand can make an impact either positive or
        negative.
      </p>
      <h2>How we approach branding</h2>
      <p>
        We offer a strategic and creative perspective to company branding. This
        involves understanding the target audience and the goals of the brand,
        and then developing a unique and cohesive brand identity that resonates
        with that audience. This can include creating the name, logo, brand
        guidelines, messaging, and visual elements that reflect the brand's
        personality and positioning. Ultimately, the goal of our branding work
        is to build awareness, credibility, and loyalty for your business.
      </p>
      <h2>Strategy Before a Style Guide</h2>
      <p>
        We learn who you serve, what makes the offer different, and which claims
        you can prove. Then we develop the identity system: naming or messaging
        where needed, logo, color, type, imagery, and usage guidance. The work
        should hold together on a website, packaging, social post, sign, and
        sales deck.
      </p>
      <h2>Give the Brand a Real Job</h2>
      <p>
        A strong identity helps customers recognize the same business across
        search, ads, ecommerce, and direct contact. It also gives writers and
        designers a useful standard as new channels appear. See how Kelp
        developed brand and digital work for SpringWater Spirits and <a href="/work/us-labels/">US Labels</a>.
        Talk with us about what your brand needs to clarify.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        Brand work becomes useful when it helps people make consistent choices.
        We translate positioning into a visual and verbal system for the
        website, campaigns, sales materials, and everyday content. That includes
        rules for use, not only polished examples. We also consider the
        business's existing recognition, so the identity can evolve without
        discarding what customers already know and trust.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Positioning and message direction</li>
        <li>Logo, typography, color, and imagery system</li>
        <li>Applications across web, print, packaging, or apparel</li>
        <li>Guidelines and production-ready assets</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        We can begin with a focused audit of the current identity and the places
        it breaks down. From there, Kelp can recommend a refinement or a fuller
        identity project.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>Do we need a new logo?</h3>
      <p>
        Not always. The larger issue may be unclear positioning or inconsistent
        use of existing assets. We define the problem before deciding which
        identity elements should change.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Let's Talk
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
